// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-07 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1087, T1082
// Tags: car.2016-03-001
// Description: Detects a set of suspicious network related commands often used in recon stages
// False positives:
//   - False positives depend on scripts and administrative tools used in the monitored environment
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/02/07/qbot-likes-to-move-it-move-it/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_nslookup_domain_discovery.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "nslookup" and ProcessCommandLine contains "_ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs."
